  "words": ["snow", "ice", "frost", "chill", "blizzard", "holiday", "fireplace", "hot chocolate"],
  "rhyme": "winter"
}
In the code, please make sure to use a rhyming dictionary API to find words that rhyme with "winter."

output:
Sure, here's the JavaScript code that generates the four-line rhyming poem using the provided JSON data:
```
const request = require('request');
const data = {
  "words": ["snow", "ice", "frost", "chill", "blizzard", "holiday", "fireplace", "hot chocolate"],
  "rhyme": "winter"
};
const rhymingDictionaryAPI = 'https://api.datamuse.com/words?rel_rhy=' + data.rhyme;
request(rhymingDictionaryAPI, { json: true }, (err, res, body) => {
  if (err) { return console.log(err); }

  const rhymingWords = body.map(word => word.word);

  const coldWord = data.words[Math.floor(Math.random() * data.words.length)];
  const rhymingWord = rhymingWords[Math.floor(Math.random() * rhymingWords.length)];

  const poem = `${coldWord} and ${data.words[Math.floor(Math.random() * data.words.length)]},\n${data.words[Math.floor(Math.random() * data.words.length)]} and ${data.words[Math.floor(Math.random() * data.words.length)]},\n${data.words[Math.floor(Math.random() * data.words.length)]} by the ${data.words[Math.floor(Math.random() * data.words.length)]},\n${rhymingWord} is here, and it's a winner.`;

  console.log(poem);
});
```
This code uses the `request` package to make an HTTP request to a rhyming dictionary API to find words that rhyme with "winter." It then selects a random word from the provided words array for the first line of the poem and a random rhyming word for the last line of the poem. The second and third lines of the poem are also randomly selected from the provided words array.
