5. Add functionality to the Go code to allow the user to filter the list of French dishes by dietary preferences and sort it alphabetically or by popularity.
Here is an example Go code that retrieves the list of French dishes and their descriptions from a MySQL database and displays it on an HTML page:
```
package main
import (
	"database/sql"
	"fmt"
	"html/template"
	"log"
	"net/http"
	_ "github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql"
)
type Dish struct {
	Name        string
	Description string
	Vegan       bool
	GlutenFree  bool
	DairyFree   bool
	Popularity  int
}
func main() {
	db, err := sql.Open("mysql", "user:password@tcp(localhost:3306)/database")
	if err != nil {
		log.Fatal(err)
	}
	defer db.Close()
	http.HandleFunc("/", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
		rows, err := db.Query("SELECT name, description, vegan, gluten_free, dairy_free, popularity FROM dishes")
		if err != nil {
			log.Fatal(err)
		}
		defer rows.Close()
		var dishes []Dish
		for rows.Next() {
			var dish Dish
			err := rows.Scan(&dish.Name, &dish.Description, &dish.Vegan, &dish.GlutenFree, &dish.DairyFree, &dish.Popularity)
			if err != nil {
				log.Fatal(err)
			}
			dishes = append(dishes, dish)
		}
		if err := rows.Err(); err != nil {
			log.Fatal(err)
		}
		tmpl := template.Must(template.ParseFiles("index.html"))
		err = tmpl.Execute(w, dishes)
		if err != nil {
			log.Fatal(err)
		}
	})
	fmt.Println("Listening on :8080")
	http.ListenAndServe(":8080", nil)
}
```
In this code, we first connect to a MySQL database using the `sql.Open` function. We then define a `Dish` struct that represents a French dish and its properties. We define a handler function for the root URL `/` that retrieves the list of dishes from the database using a SQL query and stores them in a slice of `Dish` structs. We then parse an HTML template file `index.html` that displays the list of dishes and execute it with the slice of `Dish` structs as the data. Finally, we start an HTTP server on port `8080` to serve the HTML page.
